{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And both of them shall die.</b> Rashi's comment: to include those who come after them. The explanation: lest you say, since the judgment of the adulterer and the adulteress is completed for execution, they are considered as dead, and if they came and committed adultery again — he with another woman and she with another man — you would say, since the first ones' judgment is completed for execution, they are considered as dead, and their act is not significant, as we say in general: one may not kill others on their account (the principle of גברא קטילא — a condemned man's subsequent acts are as those of a dead man). Therefore it is written <b>גם</b> here, to include those who come after them, so that we execute them for it. Another interpretation: <b>גם</b> to include those who come after them — the man who lies with another man's wife even though she is a minor, and another man's wife even though she was violated by a minor. And even though it says above that the girl alone is stoned, that is because the violator is not identifiable, but here, where the violator is identifiable, both of them die, and their manner of death is strangulation. Another interpretation: <b>both of them</b> — to include that if she is pregnant, we do not wait to execute her until she gives birth. And it is juxtaposed here in order to juxtapose the law of acts of intercourse."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "In the first interpretation, the phrase גברא קטילא קטלי (literally 'a slain man slays') is rendered according to the context: a person already condemned to death is not held accountable for further acts, so no additional death penalty can be applied. The final line דין בעילות is rendered literally; it likely refers to juxtaposing the laws of illicit intercourse found in the surrounding verses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:53:57.338827588Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}